1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,079
A cell stores energy in chemicals.

2
00:00:02,079 --> 00:00:06,713
In a closed circuit, they react and the energy is transferred by electricity.

3
00:00:06,713 --> 00:00:12,357
A battery is two or more cells joined. In the symbol, the longer line is the positive terminal.

4
00:00:13,416 --> 00:00:19,773
Connect cells in series, positive to negative, and their voltages add up: four 3-volt cells give 12 volts.

5
00:00:19,773 --> 00:00:21,911
The current capacity stays the same.

6
00:00:22,971 --> 00:00:28,852
Connect cells in parallel, and the voltage stays the same as one cell, but the capacity increases,

7
00:00:28,852 --> 00:00:30,575
so the battery lasts longer.

8
00:00:30,575 --> 00:00:35,387
Rechargeable batteries cost more at first, but are cheaper and greener over time.
